                <pb facs="0028" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg16"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 Steering Committee/547: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dearing</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-21T18:00:00-04:00">May 21, 1937—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. Legation’s 42, May 20, 10 a.m. Please express to Mr. Sandler our deep
                    appreciation for his courtesy in making this information available to us and say
                    that the interest of the United States Government in the reduction and
                    limitation of armaments has in no way abated.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Bern by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
